    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s daily efficiency scores indicate that **Lawrence Butler** is our standout play of the day (73.47). Facing Tyler Phillips, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a vulnerable rotation, paired with a significant 13% boost from his platoon advantage. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.46) and **Luis Arraez** (66.78) follow closely behind; **Jonathan Aranda** leverages a strong 0.378 xwOBA, while **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** are major beneficiaries of a favorable environment against Ryan Feltner, with park and pitcher skill factors adding double-digit percentage points to their overall outlooks. **Dylan Beavers** remains a rock-solid start (65.55) as he continues to be integrated into the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was leaving **Geraldo Perdomo** on the bench. While his score of 49.92 reflects a decent floor and a high-leverage spot in the lineup, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to the matchup against Kyle Harrison. With Harrison\u2019s xERA sitting at a sharp 2.97, the downgrade in expected run production outweighed the benefits of **Geraldo Perdomo** holding the #2 spot. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding the Catcher slots; **Yainer Diaz** (57.47) and **Cal Raleigh** (41.82) are both in \"Lineup Pending\" status, and **Cal Raleigh** in particular is flirting with our bench threshold given his difficult matchup against Dylan Cease. Monitoring the official lineup cards is essential before first pitch to ensure we aren't burning game caps on suboptimal platoon rotations.",
